From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: pm8941-pwrkey - drop repeated release after wakeup

A power key press that wakes the phone from s2idle is reported twice:
systemd-logind logs "Power key pressed short." two times for the one
press, and GNOME acts on the second one.

The interrupt is dual-edge. When the key wakes the system, the handler
runs after the key is already up, once for the replayed wakeup interrupt
and again for the release edge. Both read a released key with no press
reported before, and since "simulate missed key press events" each such
run reports a press and a release.

Treat a release without press that comes within 500 ms of the previous
release as a repeat and drop it. A live press is handled while the key is
down, so runtime presses, double taps included, are unaffected.

Status: hypothesis until tested on the OnePlus 6 (pm8998).
---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c	2026-11-19 17:08:15.165802312 +0100
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c	2026-11-19 17:08:37.047348130 +0100
@@ -54,6 +54,12 @@
 #define  PON_DBC_SHIFT_GEN1		6
 #define  PON_DBC_SHIFT_GEN2		14
 
+/*
+ * A release seen without its press this soon after the previous release is a
+ * second delivery of an edge already reported, not a new key press.
+ */
+#define PON_DUP_RELEASE_WINDOW_MS	500
+
 struct pm8941_data {
 	unsigned int	pull_up_bit;
 	unsigned int	status_bit;
@@ -80,6 +86,7 @@
 	u32 code;
 	u32 sw_debounce_time_us;
 	ktime_t sw_debounce_end_time;
+	ktime_t last_release_time;
 	bool last_status;
 	const struct pm8941_data *data;
 };
@@ -174,12 +181,26 @@
 	/*
 	 * Simulate a press event in case a release event occurred without a
 	 * corresponding press event.
+	 *
+	 * When the key wakes the system, the interrupt can be handled more
+	 * than once after the key is already up (the wakeup interrupt is
+	 * replayed on resume, and the release edge raises it again). Each run
+	 * reads a released key; simulating a press for every one of them
+	 * reports one physical press as two. Drop the repeats.
 	 */
 	if (!pwrkey->last_status && !sts) {
+		if (ktime_before(ktime_get(),
+				 ktime_add_ms(pwrkey->last_release_time,
+					      PON_DUP_RELEASE_WINDOW_MS))) {
+			dev_dbg(pwrkey->dev, "ignoring repeated release\n");
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
+		}
 		input_report_key(pwrkey->input, pwrkey->code, 1);
 		input_sync(pwrkey->input);
 	}
 	pwrkey->last_status = sts;
+	if (!sts)
+		pwrkey->last_release_time = ktime_get();
 
 	input_report_key(pwrkey->input, pwrkey->code, sts);
 	input_sync(pwrkey->input);
